---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import PageBody from "../components/PageBody.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";
import { route } from "../lib/catalogue";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "linear", label: "Linear", heading: false },
  { id: "circular", label: "Circular" },
  { id: "meter", label: "Meter" },
  { id: "colors", label: "Colors" },
]);
---
<DocsLayout page="preloader">
<p>In forced-colors mode, native and custom progress use system colors. Empty linear tracks get an outline, and circular indicators keep their value segments. Under reduced motion, the indicators still show static feedback. Browser emulation checks do not replace a review in Windows high contrast or with a screen reader.</p>

<PageBody sections={S}>
  <p>Custom linear progress fills from the left in LTR and from the right in RTL. Indeterminate motion and the static reduced-motion fill follow the inherited direction, including nested overrides. This does not change native determinate progress or circular indicators.</p>
  <Section {...S.linear}>
        <p class="flow-text">
          Show a progress indicator when content takes a while to load. A
          linear bar is a native <code>&lt;progress&gt;</code>. A circular
          spinner is one element. Both are CSS only and need no JavaScript
          plugin.
        </p>

        <h3>Linear</h3>
        <p>
          A bar with a <code>value</code> is determinate. Omit it for an
          indeterminate bar. The fill is <code>primary</code> on a
          <code>secondary-container</code> track.
        </p>

        <h5 class="light">Determinate</h5>
        <progress class="progress" value="70" max="100"></progress>
<Code code={`
<progress class="progress" value="70" max="100"></progress>
`} />
        <p>
          A <code>div</code> still works. Set the width on
          <code>.determinate</code>, or set
          <code>--md-comp-progress-value</code> on the bar.
        </p>
        <div class="progress" role="progressbar" aria-valuenow="70" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100">
          <div class="determinate" style="width: 70%"></div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="progress" role="progressbar" aria-valuenow="70" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100">
  <div class="determinate" style="width: 70%"></div>
</div>

<div class="progress" role="progressbar" aria-valuenow="70" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" style="--md-comp-progress-value: 70%"></div>
`} />

        <h5 class="light">Indeterminate</h5>
        <progress class="progress"></progress>
<Code code={`
<progress class="progress"></progress>
`} />
        <p>The child class is the alias:</p>
        <div class="progress" role="progressbar">
          <div class="indeterminate"></div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="progress" role="progressbar">
  <div class="indeterminate"></div>
</div>
`} />
        <h5 class="light">End stop and wave</h5>
        <p>
          Add <code>stop</code> to put a 4dp dot in the indicator colour at the
          track's end. It shows where the bar ends when the track has too
          little contrast with the page. Add <code>wavy</code> to draw the
          indicator as a wave over a thin track, the M3 Expressive look for a
          longer wait. The bar grows to 14px to hold the wave, and
          <code>--md-comp-progress-wavelength</code> sets its period. Both
          classes work on <code>&lt;progress&gt;</code>, a
          <code>.determinate</code> child and a bare bar. A wavy bar can also
          be indeterminate.
        </p>
        <progress class="progress stop" value="40" max="100"></progress>
        <progress class="progress wavy stop" value="60" max="100"></progress>
        <progress class="progress wavy"></progress>
<Code code={`
<progress class="progress stop" value="40" max="100"></progress>
<progress class="progress wavy stop" value="60" max="100"></progress>
<progress class="progress wavy"></progress>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.circular}>
        <p>
          For an indeterminate wait under about five seconds, prefer the
          <a href={route('loading_indicator')}>loading indicator</a>. It
          replaces the indeterminate circular spinner as the default for a
          short wait. The indeterminate spinner below still works and is not
          deprecated.
        </p>
        <p>
          The spinner is one element. The default size is 48px,
          <code>small</code> is 36px, and <code>big</code> is 64px.
          It uses the primary token, and <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>
          freezes the arc.
        </p>
        <div class="row py-5">
          <div class="s4 center-align">
            <span class="progress circular big" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="s4 center-align">
            <span class="progress circular" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="s4 center-align">
            <span class="progress circular small" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<span class="progress circular" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
<span class="progress circular small" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
<span class="progress circular big" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
`} />
        <p>
          Add <code>determinate</code> and set
          <code>--md-comp-progress-value</code> for a known percentage.
        </p>
        <p>
          <span class="progress circular determinate" style="--md-comp-progress-value: 70%" role="progressbar" aria-valuenow="70" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-label="Loading"></span>
        </p>
<Code code={`
<span class="progress circular determinate"
      style="--md-comp-progress-value: 70%"
      role="progressbar" aria-valuenow="70"
      aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100"
      aria-label="Loading"></span>
`} />
        <p>
          <code>wavy</code> draws the indicator as a wave round the ring, the
          M3 Expressive look for a longer wait. A determinate wavy ring keeps
          a thin plain track after the wave. A wavy spinner has none.
        </p>
        <p>
          <span class="progress circular wavy" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
          <span class="progress circular wavy determinate" style="--md-comp-progress-value: 65%" role="progressbar" aria-valuenow="65" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-label="Uploading"></span>
        </p>
<Code code={`
<span class="progress circular wavy" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
<span class="progress circular wavy determinate"
      style="--md-comp-progress-value: 65%"
      role="progressbar" aria-valuenow="65"
      aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100"
      aria-label="Uploading"></span>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.meter}>
        <p>
          A <code>&lt;progress&gt;</code> shows how far a task has gone. A
          <code>&lt;meter&gt;</code> shows a measurement within a known range,
          such as storage used or password strength. It needs no class. Every
          meter gets an 8px bar on a <code>secondary-container</code> track
          and fills its container's width. Set <code>width</code> on a meter
          to keep it inline.
        </p>
        <p>
          Set the native <code>low</code>, <code>high</code> and
          <code>optimum</code> attributes to choose the fill color. A value in
          the same region as <code>optimum</code> is <code>primary</code>, one
          region away is <code>tertiary</code>, and two regions away is
          <code>error</code>. In the storage example below, less is better,
          so <code>optimum</code> sits below <code>low</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <label for="meter-demo-ok">Storage used: 40 GB of 100 GB</label>
          <meter id="meter-demo-ok" min="0" max="100" low="60" high="85" optimum="0" value="40">40 GB</meter>
        </p>
        <p>
          <label for="meter-demo-warn">Storage used: 70 GB of 100 GB</label>
          <meter id="meter-demo-warn" min="0" max="100" low="60" high="85" optimum="0" value="70">70 GB</meter>
        </p>
        <p>
          <label for="meter-demo-full">Storage used: 95 GB of 100 GB</label>
          <meter id="meter-demo-full" min="0" max="100" low="60" high="85" optimum="0" value="95">95 GB</meter>
        </p>
<Code code={`
<label for="storage">Storage used: 70 GB of 100 GB</label>
<meter id="storage" min="0" max="100" low="60" high="85" optimum="0" value="70">70 GB</meter>
`} />
        <p>
          Give each meter a visible label that states the value. The color
          alone does not tell anyone whether the reading is good.
          Override <code>--md-comp-meter-track</code>,
          <code>--md-comp-meter-optimum</code>,
          <code>--md-comp-meter-suboptimum</code>,
          <code>--md-comp-meter-even-less-good</code>,
          <code>--md-comp-meter-thickness</code> and
          <code>--md-comp-meter-shape</code> to change the colors, height and
          corner radius.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.colors}>
        <p>
          The indicator follows the theme. Override
          <code>--md-comp-progress-indicator</code> to use another role.
        </p>
        <div class="row py-5">
          <div class="s3 center-align">
            <span class="progress circular" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="s3 center-align">
            <span class="progress circular" style="--md-comp-progress-indicator: var(--md-sys-color-error)" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="s3 center-align">
            <span class="progress circular" style="--md-comp-progress-indicator: var(--md-sys-color-tertiary)" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="s3 center-align">
            <span class="progress circular" style="--md-comp-progress-indicator: var(--md-sys-color-secondary)" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<span class="progress circular"
      style="--md-comp-progress-indicator: var(--md-sys-color-error)"
      role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
`} />
  </Section>
</PageBody>
</DocsLayout>
